  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Project a GJK simplex face perpendicular to its plane instead of reconstructing a cancellation-sensitive point from barycentrics.",
  "regressions": [
    "A centered cylinder penetrating a wide floor by 0.005 had a 2.697e-6 tangential simplex residual; repeated-support termination then returned a horizontal normal. The resident scene exceeded 0.02 ground penetration at frame four.",
    "Native GJK/EPA tests cover penetrating and separated floor/cylinder pairs at scales 0.1, 1, 10 and 100, requiring the correct status, vertical normal and analytic depth/gap.",
    "The required floor_cylinder GJK replay includes all eight scaled pairs; independent support/containment checks and unchanged tolerances remain active."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Rust and TileLang both retain feature selection, barycentric weights and vertex order. Only the interior face projection of a dimension-two simplex uses normal * (normal dot vertex / normal squared). Degenerate zero-normal faces retain the prior result.",
    "This changes reference behavior when barycentric reconstruction produced a spurious tangential direction near the origin; no parity tolerance is relaxed.",
    "The independent CSO decomposition checker now requires exactly rounded f32 witness subtraction, replacing a fixed f64 absolute-residual bound that rejected valid scaled geometry. A one-ULP fabrication mutation must fail."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0040-convex-projection-simplex",
    "0048-deferred-composite-collisions"
  ]
}
